      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-07-27_WidnesExaminer_art0070" n="art0070">
        <head>BABY LIKE A MUMMY. Death seemed inevitable. Mother describes Amazing Cure by DR. CASSELL'S TABLETS.</head>
        <p>BABY LIKE A MUMMY. Death seemed inevitable. Mother describes Amazing Cure by DR. CASSELL'S TABLETS.</p>
        <p>A case which shows the immeasurable superi4 of Dr. Cassell's Tablets over all ordinary drug I eines is that of little Archibald Peers, the monll baby of Mrs. Louisa Peers, of 14, May-lane, 1•;j Heath, Birmingham. Mrs. Peers says :—" My . boy began to ail when lie was a month old, and .11 wasted away. He could keep nothing on his stoma Doctors' medicine did no good, neither did patent foods ordered, and baby went on getting' and thinner till he was like a little mummy. legs and arms were Irawn up tightly against body, and his little backbone and hip bones through the skin—l mean that the skin was I broken and raw and had to be dressed. We took • to hospital, but were no more successful. Bot,l heard of Dr. Cassell's Tablets and tried them, 313 could not have believed anything could have acted r beneficially nor so quickly. In a month be via 9 improved that friends would hardly believe be the same baby." Archie is now a fine healthy boy of four. Cassell's Tablets saved his lice as they have unnumbered lives by supplying thihealing force the weakened system needs. That is why they c when nothing else will. Dr. Cassell's, Tablets for W' and Nervous People are 1/11 and 2/9 ; special size at 10.1 d , of all chemists and stores.</p>
