      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-07-27_WidnesExaminer_art0071" n="art0071">
        <head>ANGLING.</head>
        <p>ANGLING.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON WORKINGMEN'S ANGLING ASSOCIATION. (N.A. CENTRE).</p>
        <p>Although the weather last week end was tidal-, able for outside sport there were more fish recordeo the set board than any week since the seasen OP Bream, roach and trout were weighed in and the in the roach column looks pretty well used up. fell rather heavily long before train time on S 1 last and it must have damped the ardour of 1 anglers, hut those who braved the elements were paid, as the weather Chester way was not as had so Warrington. Chester, Mickle Trafford, Hera: Norton and Long Barn were visited and fair sport , general. Croefields fished their match in their ° water at Martinscroft and the winner turned out to. a Northern Angler. The bait used was bread and 136'i and it is not often we hear of a match being won this bait. Congratulations to Mr Savage. ferhaP° - will allow the members at Billings Green that mat,,c can be won with his speciality as well as wit' feeder and maggot.</p>
        <p>OPENING MATCH. The opening match at Billings Green takes Pla°e Sunday, July 23th and we are expecting a good at for £7 worth of prizes. Most of the mernberS travelling by motor ctar-a-bane. The Crewe cent? holding their match in the same length at Ward! their match being a day previous to ours and ' assured that given favourable conditions there good sport.</p>
        <p>CHESTER. Several members who visited the Dee say it improved wonderfully from the week previous. J liryers had a day out by beating his own bi weighing in a trout and filling his basket of roach, bream, trout and 'capturing a hybrid thst', described as part bream, roach and dace. The species mentioned were quite distinct and its was about 9oz. and its condition very good. members had good fish from the Dee and canal but to disturb the set board. The heaviest bream 1' here this season is 31b., 40z., 2drs. HARTFORD. c vet°l The Weaver was again well patronised. Pea, IA, v matches took place and the angling for matches v its best. Local anglers there left out of the prizesfork with over filbs. of fish, the winner having over liolf and roach was taken in the matches 7 and 8 oz. Avg toe of this description is good for the sport and give° novice the longing to become more efficient. MICKLE TRAFFORD: hoc' fc'r The Gowy's returns were better than we have - some weeks past. Several fair bags of roach wer.e iI along with dace and one member iaeighed in a pi" fot over 31bs. The eels were also more plentiful 010 some time past.</p>
      </div>
