        <p>DRUIDS' BOWLING MAIN. "SIR GILBERT GREENALL, CUP." The local Druids held their annnal wain for the "Greenall " Challenge Cup on Saturday at Sankey Chapel House Hotel. There was a capital entry includ- ing the D.D.G.M. Bro. Wm Bibby, jun., D.T. Bro, R Perdue, P.D.0.N1. Bro. S. Packer, P.N.G.A. Bro. Win Woods and P.D.G.M. Bro. John Bibby, secretary. The green was in good condition and some excellent bowl- ing was seen, especially in the final between Bro. W Goulden of Peuketh Lodge and Bro. W Thomason of Druids' Camp Lodge, The cup will be presented to the winner at a later date. FIRST Rot:ND. J Hardman, 0-1 S Woods, 0-1 Joe Bowyer, ') l3 D manning, 3 G E Durubell,3 T Hill, senior, 3 w.o. R Critchley, 3 abs. G Eastwood, 9 l3 it Perdue 5 III Job Jones, 9 l3 T Corwelf, 9 9 W Hardman, 4 l3 T Owen, 2 It Acorab. 5 A Price, 9 l3 J Bibby, 5 li G Hurrop, 5 W Woodd, 5 J Watkins, 3 I3T Wetster, 3 W Thour,sou, cc W Goulden, 1 l3 E Coyne, 5 R Barlow, 4 H Bowyers, 1 G riEddon, :3 l3 NV Barton, 9 l2 J Broadhurst sear, cc l3 A Bowyer, 1 lO 11 Massey, 2 w.o. S Davies' 9 abs. Geof Bowyer, se l3 W Fletcher, 5 W Nicholson, 5 R Graham, 1 l3 j Bowyer, 1 ll H J Mainle‘ ~ 5 w.o. J Hardman, 3 abs. J Ray, 1 l3 J Hall, 1 W H i- night, 4 W Ryder, 2 H Bingham. 3 T Gregson, 1 l3 J Ashburner, 3 W Rafters, 3 D Cooper, 9 l3 .1 J Worsley, 5 T Hill 'ten, 3 l3 10 Shy. ,Y, 1</p>
