        <p>Pure Indian Tea commands the markets of the world. India exports in a year 249,000,000 lbs. of well manufactured tea of which the United Kingdom consumes 169,000,000 lbs. So keen is the desire for the delicious teas from India that the de- mand has out-run the supply, and the dealer is tempted to keep down the price of his blends by substituting inferior teas from foreign countries for the genuine Indian product. These substitutes have neither the richness nor the purity of Indian tea. It is therefore desirable for the purchaser to obtain a guarantee that the tea sold her is genuine Indian. Considerations of economy, of health, and of comfort, unite in recommend- ing this course.</p>
